# Shell scripts must keep LF endings no matter what platform they are checked
# out on. Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default, which
# would otherwise hand docker/oracle-utplsql/init-scripts/*.sh to the Oracle
# container with CRLF line endings -- bash then fails on the carriage return
# ("/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter"), and the database comes up without utPLSQL
# installed and without the v$session grant the integration suite needs.
#
# Scoped to *.sh on purpose rather than a repo-wide `* text=auto`: the rest of
# the tree is checked out with platform-native endings today, and
# renormalising it would touch every file for no benefit.
*.sh text eol=lf
